RPT_INFO @ 0 [DEMO] 
##########################################################################
# BACKPRESSURE SCENARIOS DEMO
#
# Setup: a producer has data EVERY cycle. It feeds a FIFO of 8 entries. The
# consumer drains ONE item every 4 cycles, so the producer is 4x faster and the
# FIFO fills up. Flow-control information needs 3 cycles to reach the producer.
#
# BACKPRESSURE = the downstream side slowing the upstream side so nothing is lost and
# nothing overflows. The best possible result is 100% consumer utilisation, 0 drops.
##########################################################################
RPT_INFO @ 0 [DEMO] 
==========================================================================
 SCENARIO: NO BACKPRESSURE (producer ignores a full FIFO)
==========================================================================
  Rule : the producer ignores the FIFO state and sends every cycle.
  Risk : once the FIFO is full every further item is thrown away.
  Expect: most sent items are DROPPED; the consumer stays busy.
  narrating the first 16 cycles:
RPT_WARNING @ 11 [BP] FIFO overflow: first item lost (occupancy 8/8)
RPT_ERROR @ 200 [BP] 142 of 200 items were LOST (FIFO overflow)  [NO BACKPRESSURE (producer ignores a full FIFO)]
RPT_INFO @ 200 [DEMO] RESULT after 200 cycles:
    items sent            : 200
    items accepted        : 58
    items DROPPED (lost)  : 142   <-- DATA LOSS
    items consumed        : 50 of 50 consumer slots (100% utilisation)
    producer stall cycles : 0
    consumer idle slots   : 0   ok
    peak FIFO occupancy   : 8/8
RPT_INFO @ 0 [DEMO] 
==========================================================================
 SCENARIO: READY/VALID (immediate full indication)
==========================================================================
  Rule : the producer sends only when the FIFO has space THIS cycle.
  Gain : lossless, the simplest form of backpressure.
  Cost : needs a combinational full/ready path from the consumer side to the producer,
         which is not always possible over a long or pipelined link.
  Expect: 0 drops, consumer 100% busy, the producer is stalled most cycles.
  narrating the first 16 cycles:
RPT_INFO @ 200 [DEMO] RESULT after 200 cycles:
    items sent            : 58
    items accepted        : 58
    items DROPPED (lost)  : 0   ok
    items consumed        : 50 of 50 consumer slots (100% utilisation)
    producer stall cycles : 142
    consumer idle slots   : 0   ok
    peak FIFO occupancy   : 8/8
RPT_INFO @ 0 [DEMO] 
==========================================================================
 SCENARIO: DELAYED STALL (flag raised only when full)
==========================================================================
  Rule : a stall flag is raised only when the FIFO is FULL, and it takes 3 cycles to reach
         the producer.
  Risk : during those cycles the producer keeps sending into a FIFO that has no room left.
         Backpressure exists, but it is too late.
  Expect: fewer drops than 'none', but still DATA LOSS.
  narrating the first 16 cycles:
RPT_WARNING @ 11 [BP] FIFO overflow: first item lost (occupancy 8/8)
RPT_ERROR @ 200 [BP] 24 of 81 items were LOST (FIFO overflow)  [DELAYED STALL (flag raised only when full)]
RPT_INFO @ 200 [DEMO] RESULT after 200 cycles:
    items sent            : 81
    items accepted        : 57
    items DROPPED (lost)  : 24   <-- DATA LOSS
    items consumed        : 50 of 50 consumer slots (100% utilisation)
    producer stall cycles : 119
    consumer idle slots   : 0   ok
    peak FIFO occupancy   : 8/8
RPT_INFO @ 0 [DEMO] 
==========================================================================
 SCENARIO: WATERMARK (early stall with headroom + hysteresis)
==========================================================================
  Rule : the same 3-cycle flag, but raised EARLY at a high watermark (capacity - latency)
         and released at a low watermark (half of the high one).
  Why it works: the free entries above the high watermark absorb the items that are still
         in flight; the gap between the two marks avoids flag chatter (hysteresis) and keeps
         enough items queued for the consumer while the release travels back.
  Expect: 0 drops, consumer 100% busy, peak occupancy below capacity.
  narrating the first 16 cycles:
RPT_INFO @ 200 [DEMO] RESULT after 200 cycles:
    items sent            : 56
    items accepted        : 56
    items DROPPED (lost)  : 0   ok
    items consumed        : 50 of 50 consumer slots (100% utilisation)
    producer stall cycles : 144
    consumer idle slots   : 0   ok
    peak FIFO occupancy   : 6/8
RPT_INFO @ 0 [DEMO] 
==========================================================================
 SCENARIO: CREDIT-BASED (credits = capacity)
==========================================================================
  Rule : the producer owns one credit per FIFO entry. Sending costs a credit, each consumer
         pop returns one 3 cycles later. The FIFO can never overflow.
  Gain : lossless by construction, works over any link latency.
  Expect: 0 drops, consumer 100% busy.
  narrating the first 16 cycles:
RPT_INFO @ 200 [DEMO] RESULT after 200 cycles:
    items sent            : 57
    items accepted        : 57
    items DROPPED (lost)  : 0   ok
    items consumed        : 50 of 50 consumer slots (100% utilisation)
    producer stall cycles : 143
    consumer idle slots   : 0   ok
    peak FIFO occupancy   : 8/8
RPT_INFO @ 0 [DEMO] 
==========================================================================
 SCENARIO: CREDIT-BASED (under-provisioned: 1 credit, 6-cycle return)
==========================================================================
  Rule : same scheme, but only ONE credit and a 6-cycle credit return.
  Risk : the producer can only have one item in flight per credit round trip, which is longer
         than the consumer's drain interval, so the FIFO runs dry.
  Expect: 0 drops (still safe) but the consumer wastes slots: THROUGHPUT LOSS, not data loss.
  narrating the first 16 cycles:
RPT_WARNING @ 200 [BP] consumer wasted 25 slot(s) on an empty FIFO: the flow-control loop is too slow or under-provisioned
RPT_INFO @ 200 [DEMO] RESULT after 200 cycles:
    items sent            : 25
    items accepted        : 25
    items DROPPED (lost)  : 0   ok
    items consumed        : 25 of 50 consumer slots (50% utilisation)
    producer stall cycles : 175
    consumer idle slots   : 25   <-- bubbles
    peak FIFO occupancy   : 1/8
RPT_INFO @ 200 [DEMO] 
TAKEAWAY
  NO BACKPRESSURE : overflow, data is lost.
  LATE BACKPRESSURE: a stall that is only raised when the FIFO is full still overflows;
                     the signal latency must be covered by headroom (watermarks) or credits.
  TOO MUCH CAUTION: too few credits (or a watermark that is too low) never loses data but
                     starves the consumer. Size the buffer for the round-trip latency:
                     capacity >= flow-control latency + items needed to keep the consumer busy.

